# i18n Management Rules

## Overview

Translation **authoring** lives in `packages/i18n-catalog/`:

- `*/originals/` — en-US hand-maintained; other locales LLM-generated
- `*/overrides/` — human corrections (empty string = use originals)
- `*/compiled/` — per-layer build output (gitignored)

Apps load **merged** output from `apps/*/i18n/compiled/` at runtime (generated by
`npm run i18n:compile`).

## Catalog layers

| Layer | Use for |
| ----- | ------- |
| `shared/` | Cross-app: `language.*`, shared `errors.*`, shared `misc.*`, `settings.ui_theme.*` |
| `consumer/` | Web + mobile consumer namespaces |
| `management/` | Management-web only |
| `mobile/` | Mobile-only overlay (may be `{}`) |

Do **not** add `originals/` or `overrides/` under `apps/*/i18n/`.

## Apps with i18n runtime

- `apps/web` — next-intl, loads `shared + consumer` compiled merge
- `apps/management-web` — next-intl, loads `shared + management` compiled merge
- `apps/mobile` — i18next, loads `shared + consumer + mobile` compiled merge

## Shared UI (`packages/ui`)

User-facing copy lives in apps — not in `@podverse/ui`. When strings move into message
files, update the correct catalog layer (see **`shared-ui-i18n`** rule).

## Brand name and domain (no hardcoded product name)

Do **not** hardcode the product brand name (e.g. `Podverse`) or deployment domain (e.g.
`podverse.fm`) in catalog `originals/` or `overrides/`. White-label deployments set these via
env / runtime config.

| Interpolation | Env / runtime source | Pass at `t()` call site |
| ------------- | -------------------- | ----------------------- |
| `{brand_name}` | `BRAND_NAME` → `NEXT_PUBLIC_BRAND_NAME` (web/management-web sidecar) | `config.public.brand.name` (server or `useConfig()` on client) |
| `{brand_domain}` | `BRAND_DOMAIN` → `NEXT_PUBLIC_BRAND_DOMAIN` | `config.public.brand.domain` |
| `{legal_name}` | `LEGAL_NAME` → `NEXT_PUBLIC_LEGAL_NAME` | `config.public.legal.name` (where used) |

## Required locales

Keep in sync in `packages/i18n-catalog/scripts/i18n-validate.ts` and
`packages/i18n-catalog/scripts/i18n-translate.ts` (`TARGETS` / `REQUIRED_LOCALES`).

**Current locales**: `en-US`, `es`, `fr`, `el-GR`

Root `npm run i18n:validate` delegates to `@podverse/i18n-catalog`. `scripts/ci/validate-i18n.ts`
is a compatibility wrapper only.

## Adding a new locale

1. Add to `TARGETS` in `packages/i18n-catalog/scripts/i18n-translate.ts`
2. Add to `REQUIRED_LOCALES` in `packages/i18n-catalog/scripts/i18n-validate.ts`
3. Update [docs/localization/I18N.md](/docs/localization/I18N.md)
4. Run `npm run i18n:all`

## Adding new translation keys

1. Add the key to the correct layer's `packages/i18n-catalog/<layer>/originals/en-US.json`
2. Commit and merge to `develop`
3. `.github/workflows/i18n.yml` auto-translates other locales when any layer `en-US.json` changes
4. Override files sync on compile (new keys get empty override slots)

## Automated translation workflow

When `packages/i18n-catalog/*/originals/en-US.json` changes on `develop`:

- `.github/workflows/i18n.yml` runs translate → compile → validate
- Commits only catalog `originals/` and `overrides/` (not `compiled/`)

**Requires**: `OPENAI_API_KEY` repository secret.

## Commands (from repo root)

| Command | Purpose |
| ------- | ------- |
| `npm run i18n:all` | Translate + compile |
| `npm run i18n:translate` | LLM translate all layers |
| `npm run i18n:compile` | Sync overrides + write app compiled output |
| `npm run i18n:validate` | Validate catalog layers |

## Special case: packages/notifications

TypeScript-based translations in `packages/notifications/src/services/notifications/i18nNotifications.ts`
— not part of the JSON catalog. Add locales manually there when needed.

## Critical: keep files in sync

When changing i18n:

- Edit catalog layer `originals/` (and `overrides/` for human fixes)
- Run `npm run i18n:compile` before local app dev/build if compiled output is missing
- See [packages/i18n-catalog/README.md](/packages/i18n-catalog/README.md) and **i18n-catalog-layers** rule
